.TH MADEIRA-AOL 1 "November 2026" "madeira-aol 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
madeira-aol \- forward PC keyboard, mouse, and gamepad input over LAN to Madeira
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B madeira-aol
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B madeira-aol
captures local keyboard, relative mouse, and game controller events on a desktop
computer and streams them over UDP to Madeira running Accessories Over LAN (AoL)
on iOS or iPadOS. Controller vibration feedback sent by Madeira is forwarded back
to connected PC controllers.
.PP
While capture is active on Linux or Windows, pressing
.B Ctrl+Alt+G
toggles exclusive keyboard and mouse grab.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-discover
Broadcast a discovery probe on the LAN, print responding Madeira devices, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target =\fIHOST[:PORT]\fR
Connect to Madeira at \fIHOST\fR (default port 37419 if omitted).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port =\fIPORT\fR
UDP port used for discovery or default target connections (default 37419).
.TP
.BR \-\-pin =\fIPIN\fR
Four-digit or passphrase PIN matching Madeira's AoL settings.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-keyboard
Do not forward keyboard events.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Do not forward mouse motion, buttons, or wheel events.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gamepad
Do not forward gamepad input or rumble.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-grab
Read input devices without taking an exclusive desktop grab.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rumble
Ignore incoming rumble packets from Madeira.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit discovery results as JSON to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-color =\fIWHEN\fR
Colorize diagnostics: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print detailed connection, packet, and device diagnostics to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version and license information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Network, device, authentication, or runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
